  "text" : "The goal is not to keep agents busy.\nIt's to maximize the rate at which you can understand things.\nA while back I made a video about how I use Obsidian to keep agents working for me.\nBut the bottleneck has become me reviewing and understanding everything.\nNow sometimes it's useful to optimize your output,\nbut other times you want to go slow so you can deliberately understand things.\nWhen I'm working through Karpathy's LLM lecture course,\nthe agent writes the plumbing, but I write the core idea myself.\nThat's the part I want to understand.\nSo go fast on the parts that teach you nothing,\nbut go slow on the core part that you're meant to struggle with.\nNow, AI can't make you smarter on its own. You have to do that work.\nKeeping them busy is not the goal. Make sure you carve out time for your own growth.\nBlock a slot on your day where you do the work, where you write something by hand,\nread it slowly, do the deep thinking, and are not just trying to keep agents busy."
